---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site.config.js';
---

<Page
  title="Cookie policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lede="A short page, because this site uses very few cookies."
  updated="29 August 2026"
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} sets <strong>no analytics, advertising, profiling or social media cookies</strong>. There is no
    tracking pixel on this site and no third-party script that follows you elsewhere. That is why you are not being
    shown a consent banner: there is nothing here to consent to.
  </p>

  <h2>What may be set</h2>
  <h3>Strictly necessary cookies</h3>
  <p>
    Our host, Cloudflare, may set a security cookie (commonly <code>__cf_bm</code>, and in some cases
    <code>cf_clearance</code>) to distinguish human visitors from automated traffic and to protect the site from
    abuse. These are strictly necessary for the site to be served securely, are short-lived, and are not used to
    profile you or to advertise to you. Under UK and EU rules, strictly necessary cookies do not require consent.
  </p>

  <h3>Nothing else</h3>
  <p>
    We set no cookies of our own for preferences, sessions or measurement. The site's light and dark appearance
    follows your operating system setting and is not stored anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party content</h2>
  <p>
    We do not embed videos, maps, comment systems, fonts loaded from third-party servers, or social media widgets, so
    none of those set cookies here. Links to external sources open on those sites, which have their own cookie
    practices — following a citation to a newspaper means entering that newspaper's cookie regime, not ours.
  </p>

  <h2>Controlling cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking Cloudflare's security cookie may cause the
    site's protection layer to challenge your requests more often, but the content will still be readable.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. See also our
    <a href="/legal/privacy/"> privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
